{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"targets SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state graph"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — computed properties, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag"},{"type":"text","text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-four-rules","text":"The four rules","type":"heading"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"gesture + ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"@GestureState","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" + update logic","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(.spring)"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"code":"View","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" body. Origami "},{"code":"Transition","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s "},{"code":".transition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier — that’s a different concept)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property","text":"Pure value patch → computed property","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Add","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Transition\/interpolate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property (or an inline expression) — no "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", no side effect."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"down"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"position"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDoubleTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onLongPress"},{"type":"text","text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose output lands in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" or fires a callback. The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction"},{"type":"text","text":" helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture arbitration clean."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Switch"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sample and Hold"},{"type":"text","text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"callback, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onChange"},{"type":"text","text":", or an assignment inside a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" block).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", and other animation patches drive a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier on the animated property."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","text":"Flag, don’t fake","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absolute-position layout.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings"},"abstract":[{"text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"],"generated":true,"title":"Reference","anchor":"Reference"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings"},"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Beats":{"type":"topic","title":"Beats","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four-beat discipline that keeps the translator honest: one pattern per branch,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compile-clean before opening a PR, visual gate against Origami’s own render, ship","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only on Reviewer approval plus a human spot-check.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/beats","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","title":"Drag","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Drag","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" patch ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drag"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/drag","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drag"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","kind":"symbol","title":"Interaction","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction"}]},{"type":"text","text":" patch."}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"Swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","url":"\/documentation\/swami","type":"topic"}}}